ent-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:7cefc8935553adab56ca3233401ca1f24b61cef612af0ad2ef96437f7ce1ca0e","file":"preprints/Vanishing-of-higher-bounded-Hochschild-cohomology-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":192,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"846292e4359b98ae0c260c5a20c6a6c750d2ee18e6318e7638632ed66bccfba5","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Vanishing-of-higher-bounded-Hochschild-cohomology-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7cefc8935553adab56ca3233401ca1f24b61cef612af0ad2ef96437f7ce1ca0e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Vanishing-of-higher-bounded-Hochschild-cohomology-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L192"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:classical}\nLet \\(M\\) be a von Neumann algebra and \\(k\\geq2\\).\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item If \\(f\\in C_b^k(M,M)\\) is a cocycle, there are a separately\nnormal bounded cocycle \\(f_0\\) and a bounded \\((k-1)\\)-cochain \\(b\\)\nsuch that \\(f=f_0+db\\).\n\\item If \\(M\\) has no type \\(\\mathrm{II}_1\\) central summand, then\n\\(H_b^k(M,M)=0\\).\n\\end{enumerate}"}
